kens":11784.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":30001.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":1233.0,"requests":4}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","vague/subjective terms present: etc."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm the AC-checkbox precheck sits on the shared close seam (the close `*_core` write / `_seam.append_event` path or the same dispatch all ingress funnels through) so MCP and the `rebar.transition` library facade inherit it, or state explicitly that transition_close's verifier-dispatch is the single shared close path for all three surfaces.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T6","T9","project.engine-layer-enforcement"],"criteria":["project.engine-layer-enforcement"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Verbatim placement: 'src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py (precheck family, alongside _completion_precheck)'","Approach: 'In the close transition path (before the LLM verifier dispatch), parse the ticket description's ## Acceptance Criteria section'","Bypassing ingress paths: the MCP close/transition tool handler (mcp_server.py) and the `rebar.transition` library facade, which reach the same close transition/write"],"finding":"The plan places the new AC-checkbox close guard inside `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py` (a CLI command surface), 'alongside _completion_precheck' and 'before the LLM verifier dispatch'. Unless that close path is the single shared seam every ingress funnels through, the MCP `transition`/close tool handler and the `rebar.transition` library facade could reach the same close transition without passing through this precheck — letting a ticket with unchecked AC boxes be closed via MCP or the library facade, bypassing the deterministic guard.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2c165b74b0d56dd0","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope: 'src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py (precheck family, alongside _completion_precheck)' / Approach: 'In the close transition path (before the LLM verifier dispatch)'","norm_id":"n976222be86e4b4a8","priority":0.1889,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["MCP tool call: an agent issues the close transition via the MCP `transition` tool; if that handler does not route through transition_close._completion_precheck, the AC-checkbox guard is skipped and the unchecked-box close succeeds pre-verifier.","Library facade: `rebar.transition(...)` to close is called directly; the AC precheck is skippable, admitting a close with unchecked non-attested boxes.","CLI-only enforcement means the invariant ('no unchecked AC at close') is not durably enforced for every surface."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Verify whether `_completion_precheck` / the LLM verifier dispatch is invoked from a shared close-core function reached by CLI, MCP, and library facade; if so, place the AC precheck there (delegating message formatting to interfaces). If transition_close.py is CLI-only, move the guard into the shared close `*_core` seam so every ingress path enforces it automatically.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that the precheck reuses the existing AC-checkbox parser (`_plan_clarity.evaluate_plan_clarity(...).unchecked_ac_lines`, or `det_operator_attested.ac_item_lines`) rather than a new bespoke section/checkbox parser, so section/checkbox detection cannot drift from the clarity floor.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The plan mandates reuse only for the tag matcher: 'reuse the exact matcher (det_operator_attested._OPERATOR_ATTESTED_TAG_RE ...) rather than a parallel regex, so the two surfaces cannot drift' — but says nothing about reusing an AC-section/checkbox parser.","An AC-checkbox parser already exists: `evaluate_plan_clarity(...).unchecked_ac_lines` scopes checkbox detection to `## Acceptance Criteria` via `_CHECKBOX_RE` (src/rebar/_plan_clarity.py:150-170, field defined at :51).","A section-scoped AC checklist-line reader also exists: `det_operator_attested.ac_item_lines` (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_operator_attested.py:25-37).","By the plan's own drift rationale, a second bespoke definition of 'the AC section' / 'an unchecked box' is exactly the drift surface it aims to avoid for the tag match."],"finding":"For the AC-section + checkbox parsing (as opposed to the attested-tag match), the plan does not commit to reusing the existing canonical parser and risks building a parallel one, rebuilding functionality already in the codebase (NIH / drift).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fab3e24c065d11213","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan 'Approach' — 'parse the ticket description's ## Acceptance Criteria section; if any - [ ] checkbox remains unchecked'","norm_id":"ndfe3d61a468103e4","priority":0.0293,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["A future edit changes where the '## Acceptance Criteria' section is deemed to end (e.g. nested headings / fenced code), and the close precheck and the plan-clarity floor disagree on which lines are AC checkboxes.","A '- [ ]' inside a fenced code block under the AC heading is counted by one parser but not the other."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"In Approach, add: 'derive the unchecked AC lines from `_plan_clarity.evaluate_plan_clarity(description).unchecked_ac_lines` (the same parser the clarity floor uses), then filter out lines matching `_OPERATOR_ATTESTED_TAG_RE`' — i.e. reuse both existing surfaces, adding no new AC-section parsing.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1111,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing"